# .cursorrules — coding-agent-eval-harness
# Owner: Sebastien Henry. Anchor: Cursor / Harvey / Anthropic FDE portfolio.

You are pairing with a senior engineer. Write production code. No explanations unless asked.

## Stack (pinned Jun 2026)
- Python 3.12.4. uv 0.5.x. ruff 0.8.4 (select=ALL, ignore=[D,ANN101,COM812,ISC001]).
- mypy 1.13 --strict. pydantic 2.9 with ConfigDict(frozen=True, extra="forbid").
- httpx 0.28 async only. No requests, no urllib.
- Docker SDK docker==7.1.0 for container management. Never subprocess("docker ...").
- tree-sitter 0.23 for AST analysis. radon 6.0.1 for complexity.
- sentence-transformers 3.3.1 for contamination embeddings. Model: all-MiniLM-L6-v2.
- anthropic 0.40.0 (claude-sonnet-4-5-20251022 for judge, claude-opus-4-7 for hard eval).
- openai 1.53.0 for Codex baseline.
- langsmith 0.2.10 for run tracing (optional, activated by LANGSMITH_API_KEY).

## Architecture invariants
- Every agent adapter implements agents.base.AgentAdapter ABC.
- Every task runs in a FRESH Docker container via sandbox.runner.DockerSandbox.
  Never run agent code or tests on the host filesystem.
- Rubric scores are floats in [0.0, 1.0]. Composite = weighted sum defined in
  rubric/scorer.py::WEIGHTS. Changing weights requires updating docs/rubric_design.md.
- Contamination flag (is_contaminated: bool) is ALWAYS computed and stored with
  each TaskResult. Never drop contaminated tasks — flag them, include them, report
  the contamination rate separately.
- Every TaskResult carries: task_id, agent_id, patch, test_pass_rate,
  diff_minimality, complexity_delta, style_score, semantic_score, composite_score,
  is_contaminated, latency_ms, cost_usd, error (str | None).

## Security invariants (Docker sandbox)
- Sandbox containers run with: --network=none, --memory=512m, --cpus=1.0,
  --read-only (except /workspace), --tmpfs /tmp:size=64m. Never --privileged.
- No API keys passed into sandbox containers. Agent API calls happen on the host;
  only the resulting patch string enters the container.
- Timeout: 120s hard limit per container. SIGKILL after timeout.

## Contamination contract
- Contamination check uses cosine similarity of task embedding vs SWE-bench train
  set embeddings (all-MiniLM-L6-v2, pre-computed in data/contamination/).
- Threshold: similarity > 0.85 => is_contaminated = True.
- Always report: n_total, n_contaminated, contamination_rate in leaderboard output.
- Never filter contaminated tasks from eval — report separate clean/all metrics.

## Forbidden patterns
- subprocess("docker ...) or subprocess("git ...") in src/ — use Docker SDK / GitPython.
- print() in src/ — use structlog.
- time.sleep in async code — asyncio.sleep.
- Hardcoded repo names / commit SHAs in src/ — always parameterized.
- Any eval that cannot be reproduced bit-for-bit from the same task JSONL file.
  Seeds are mandatory. Model temperature = 0 for judge calls.

## Testing
- 85% line coverage gate. pytest-asyncio strict mode.
- Sandbox tests marked @pytest.mark.sandbox — require Docker, skipped in CI by default.
- Unit tests mock Docker SDK and agent API calls via respx / unittest.mock.

## Conventional commits: feat(rubric):, fix(sandbox):, chore(dataset):, etc.